#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-task-management.rst:7
msgid ""
"Mattermost Boards provides tight integration between project management "
"and Mattermost to align, define, organize, track, and manage work across "
"teams."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-task-management.rst:24
msgid "With Boards you can:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-task-management.rst:26
msgid ""
"**Manage projects and organize tasks:** A familiar kanban board structure"
" integrated with channel-based communication."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-task-management.rst:27
msgid ""
"**Manage and collaborate on various projects:** Software releases, "
"product launches, meetings, personal to-do’s, events, etc."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-task-management.rst:28
msgid ""
"**Stay on schedule:** Clearly-defined tasks, owners, checklists, "
"deadlines, and calendars."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-task-management.rst:29
msgid ""
"**Increase transparency and keep everybody in the loop:** Everything your"
" team needs in one place, including documents, images, and links that are"
" visible to every stakeholder."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-task-management.rst:32
msgid "Install Boards"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-task-management.rst:34
msgid ""
"Your system admin may need to install and enable Mattermost Boards before"
" you can use it. See the :doc:`install Mattermost Boards "
"</administration-guide/configure/install-boards>` documentation to learn "
"how to install and configure the Boards plugin for your Mattermost "
"instance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-task-management.rst:37
msgid "What's a board?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-task-management.rst:39
msgid ""
"A board is a collection of cards to help you manage your projects, "
"organize tasks, and collaborate with your team all in one place."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-task-management.rst:41
msgid ""
"Boards can be displayed and filtered in different views such as kanban, "
"table, calendar, and gallery views to help you visualize work items in "
"the format that makes most sense to you. Learn about :doc:`working with "
"boards </end-user-guide/project-management/work-with-boards>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-task-management.rst:44
msgid "What's a card?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-task-management.rst:46
msgid ""
"Cards are used on a board to track individual work items. Cards are "
"customizable and can have a number of properties added to them, which are"
" then used as a way to tag, sort, and filter the cards."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-task-management.rst:48
msgid ""
"When working with cards, you can manage properties, add descriptions, "
"attach images, assign them to team members, mention team members, add "
"comments, and so on. Learn more about :doc:`working with cards </end-"
"user-guide/project-management/work-with-cards>`."
msgstr ""

